<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela's Sivensa expects $570 mln loan by Sept.</title>
<headline>Venezuela's Sivensa expects $570 mln loan by Sept.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Venezuelan steel company Sivensa expects a long-awaited $570 million loan for construction of a new steel plant to be ready by September for production to begin in 1999, a company executive said.</p>
<p>The $700 million Finmet plant will produce 2.2 million metric tonnes per year of hot briquetted iron under a joint venture with Australia's company Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;At the moment, we reckon the financing should be ready by September this year,&quot; Sivensa's finance director Neil Malloy told reporters. The loan will be backed the U.S.'s Eximbank, Germany's Hermes and Australia's OKD, he added.</p>
<p>((-- Ana Isabel Martinez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
